.TH "PAY_RESPECTS" "1" "April 2026" "pay\-respects 0.8.8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pay\-respects \- Blazing fast terminal command suggestions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]pay\-respects\f[R] [\f[I]shell\-binary\f[R]] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
\f[B]pay\-respects\f[R] \(enmigrate\-rules \f[I]file\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
pay\-respects is a terminal suggestion tool that fixes your previous or
current typed command, with a sub\-millisecond (<1ms) performance.
.PP
The optional positional argument is the shell executable.
Its type is detected from the name.
Use \f[CR]\-\-shell\-type\f[R] when the name does not contain a known
shell name, for example
\f[CR]pay\-respects zsh\-fork \-\-shell\-type zsh\f[R].
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\-h, \(enhelp
Show help message and exit.
.TP
\(enalias
Set a custom alias instead of \f[CR]f\f[R]
.TP
\-s, \(enshell\-type <type>
Shell type when the binary name differs, such as \f[CR]zsh\-fork\f[R].
The type is detected from the binary name when omitted.
.TP
\(enmigrate\-rules <file>
Convert a version 1 rule file to version 2 on \f[CR]stdout\f[R].
.TP
\(ennocnf
Disable command\-not\-found handler
.SH INITIALIZATION
.SS Bash / Zsh / Fish / Dash
Add the following line to your configuration file:
.IP
.EX
eval \(dq$(pay\-respects bash \-\-alias)\(dq
eval \(dq$(pay\-respects zsh \-\-alias)\(dq
pay\-respects fish \-\-alias \f[B]|\f[R] source
eval \(dq$(pay\-respects dash \-\-alias)\(dq
.EE
.PP
Dash has no inline mode or command\-not\-found handler.
.SS Xonsh
Add the following line to \f[CR]\(ti/.xonshrc\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
execx($(pay\-respects xonsh \-\-alias), \(aqexec\(aq, __xonsh__.ctx, filename=\(aqpay\-respects\(aq)
.EE
.PP
Inline mode requires prompt_toolkit.
.SS Elvish
Add the following line to \f[CR]\(ti/.config/elvish/rc.elv\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
eval (pay\-respects elvish \-\-alias | slurp)
.EE
.PP
Inline mode is bound to \f[CR]Ctrl\-X\f[R].
Elvish has no command\-not\-found handler.
.SS Nushell / PowerShell
Add the following output to your configuration file.
Replace the shell with the actual executable name if needed.
.IP
.EX
pay\-respects nu
pay\-respects pwsh
.EE
.SH USAGE
Fix your previous command
.IP
.EX
f
.EE
.PP
Fix your current typed command
.IP
.EX
<C\-x> <C\-x>
.EE
.SH Examples
.IP
.EX
gitcommit + <Cr> + f + <Cr> \-\-> git commit
gitcommit + <C\-X> + <C\-X>   \-\-> git commit
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.SS Required
.TP
_PR_SHELL
The binary name of the current working shell
.TP
_PR_LAST_COMMAND
The last command
.SS Optional
.TP
_PR_SHELL_TYPE
The shell type when it differs from the binary name.
Detected from \f[CR]_PR_SHELL\f[R] if absent
.TP
_PR_ALIAS
A list of aliases to commands.
Separated by newlines with zsh\-like formatting,
e.g.\ \f[CR]gc=git commit\f[R]
.TP
_PR_ERROR_MSG
Error message from the previous command.
\f[CR]pay\-respects\f[R] will rerun previous command to get the error
message if absent
.TP
_PR_EXECUTABLES
A space separated list of commands/executables.
\f[CR]pay\-respects\f[R] will search for \f[CR]$PATH\f[R] if absent
.TP
_PR_LIB
Directory of modules, analogous to \f[CR]PATH\f[R].
If not provided, search in \f[CR]PATH\f[R] or compile\-time provided
value
.TP
_PR_PACKAGE_MANAGER
Use defined package manager instead of auto\-detecting alphabetically.
Empty value disables package search functionality
.TP
_PR_MODE
Execution mode.
.SS Configuration
.TP
_PR_PREFIX
Shell prompt prefix, required for log capture from terminal multiplexers
.TP
_PR_NO_DESPERATE
Disable desperate functions, which are slow but can give better results
.TP
_PR_NO_CONFIG
Don\(cqt load configurations
.TP
_PR_NO_ZOXIDE:
Don\(cqt use zoxide
.TP
_PR_NO_MULTIPLEXER
Equivalent of turning all the followings: \f[CR]_PR_NO_TMUX\f[R],
\f[CR]_PR_NO_SCREEN\f[R], \f[CR]_PR_NO_ZELLIJ\f[R],
\f[CR]_PR_NO_WEZTERM\f[R], \f[CR]_PR_NO_KITTY\f[R]
